# Factory pipeline

Channel: **Before It Was Famous** (`@beforeitwasfamous`). FocusStack is a Level-2 natural close, never an ad, never the story.

Would someone watch this if FocusStack did not exist? If no, reject the story.

## Command

```bash
pnpm factory <stage> --episode <slug>
pnpm factory run --episode <slug> --until <stage>
pnpm factory status --episode <slug>
```

Never skip: discover → score (≥70, pivotal ≥3/5, two reliable sources, fits ≤50s) → research spine → **FACT_APPROVED** → 2–4 hooks → script → TTS + measure → **NARRATION_LOCKED** → storyboard 8–12 beats → stills → Remotion assemble → karaoke from FINAL audio → QA → package.

`publish` refuses unless `PUBLISH_GO` exists, and still does not post. Never auto-publish. No social APIs.

## Human gates (files)

| File | When |
| --- | --- |
| `episodes/<slug>/FACT_APPROVED` | After sourced research. Script stage refuses without it (except `_fixture-*`). |
| `episodes/<slug>/NARRATION_LOCKED` | After listening to `audio/vo_concat.wav`. Storyboard refuses without it. |
| `episodes/<slug>/PUBLISH_GO` | Human publish intent. Publish stub still will not upload. |

## Facts

Never invent facts. Mock LLM returns stubs. Production claims need source ids. `FACT_APPROVED` is a hard gate.

## VO is source of truth

Duration comes from audio. Script ≠ N Remotion stills. Karaoke does not rewrite spoken words.

## Fixture

`pnpm factory run --episode _fixture-pipeline --until qa`

If Remotion/ffmpeg are missing, the render stage prints the command and writes `render/skipped.json`.
